,"s":"Service · Slimming","k":"Body Contouring · Cryolipolysis · Full Body · Slimming · Cryolipolysis / CoolSculpting System · 2 sessions · Custom · 4D Cryo(SEP OFFER)"},{"p":"pg-body","t":"Body Transformation Programme","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Slimming","k":"Clients with localised stubborn fat, loose skin after weight change, or a target event date. NSLS cavitation and RF, cryolipolysis, HIFU body, EMS toning, lymphatic drainage, inch-loss wraps, BCA tracking and a nutrition plan. Starter Slim Plan · Smart Slim Plan · Premium Body Sculpt Programme · Total Body Transformation"},{"p":"pg-glp1","t":"Medical Weight Loss / GLP-1 Programme","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Slimming","k":"BMI above 30, or age 27+ with a weight-related comorbidity, where diet and exercise alone have not worked. Doctor consultation, baseline blood panel, GLP-1 prescription and monthly titration, monthly monitoring, dietician support, body composition tracking and adjunct contouring treatments. Starter Medical Weight Loss Plan · Smart Fat Loss Programme · Obesity Reversal Programme · Premium Wedding Transformation Programme"},{"p":"pg-skin","t":"Advanced Skin Correction & Glow","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Skin","k":"Pigmentation, melasma, acne scarring, dullness, open pores and uneven tone. Q-Switch laser toning, carbon laser peel, chemical peels, Cosmelan, HydraFacial, MNRF, derma pen and skin boosters, with a prescribed home regimen. Skin Reset Plan · Skin Repair Plan · Advanced Skin Transformation · Premium Glass Skin Programme"},{"p":"pg-age","t":"Age Reverse & Glow Programme","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Skin","k":"Fine lines, laxity, jowling and loss of firmness — typically 35 and above. HIFU face and neck, RF face tightening, MNRF, skin boosters, Botox, dermal fillers and thread lift, sequenced across the plan period. Glow Starter Plan · Anti-Ageing Essential Plan · Age Reversal Plan · Premium Youth Transformation Plan"},{"p":"pg-iv","t":"Full Body Glow & Age Reverse (IV Drip)","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Skin","k":"Overall skin brightening and antioxidant support alongside a topical or laser programme. Doctor pre-drip assessment, glutathione and Vitamin C infusions, skin boosters and a maintenance regimen. Glow Starter Plan · Radiance Boost Plan · Full Body Transformation · Premium Glass Skin & Glow"},{"p":"pg-hair","t":"Hair Recovery & Regrowth Programme","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Hair","k":"Pattern hair loss, diffuse thinning, post-partum and post-illness hair fall. Trichoscopy, blood investigations, PRP or GFC, scalp therapy, mesotherapy, low-level laser and a prescribed home regimen. Basic Hair Rescue Plan · Advance Hair Care Plan · Hair Regrowth Transformation · Premium Hair Rebirth Programme"},{"p":"pg-ht","t":"Hair Transformation & HT Programme","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Hair Transplant","k":"Advanced pattern baldness with an adequate donor zone, or clients wanting a defined hairline restored. Surgeon consultation and donor assessment, pre-operative screening, FUE hair transplant, post-operative care protocol, PRP or GFC graft support and long-term medical therapy. Basic Hair Restore Plan · Advance Hair Transformation · Hair Rebirth Programme · Premium Marriage Transformation"},{"p":"pg-smooth","t":"Smooth Skin & Clear Glow (LHR + Laser)","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Laser","k":"Unwanted hair together with pigmentation, tan or uneven tone. Diode laser hair removal across chosen areas, laser toning, carbon peel and a maintenance plan. Starter Glow Plan · Smooth Skin Plan · Clear Skin Transformation · Premium Glass Skin Programme"},{"p":"pg-pmu","t":"PMU Beauty Transformation","g":"prog","s":"Programme · Aesthetics","k":"Sparse or asymmetric brows, lip colour correction, and clients wanting a defined everyday look without daily makeup. Patch test, design consultation, microblading or machine PMU, lip micropigmentation and the mandatory touch-up. Basic PMU Plan · Signature PMU Plan · Glam Transformation Plan · Premium Beauty Forever Plan"},{"p":"pg-rise","t":"LIFE RISE — Online Nutrition & Medical Programme","g":"prog","s":"Programme · LIFE RISE","k":"Clients who want a medically supervised weight and wellness programme delivered largely online, with or without in-clinic treatments. Doctor video consultation, blood tests, personalised nutrition plan, GLP-1 medical supervision where indicated, physiotherapist and psychologist support, yoga and Zumba groups, WhatsApp support and progress tracking. Higher tiers add in-clinic HydraFacial, MNRF, NSLS, cryo, HIFU and RF sessions. LIFE RISE P1 · LIFE RISE P2 · LIFE RISE P3 · LIFE RISE Online"},{"p":"ho-body","t":"Body Contouring — Before & After Your Session","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Cryolipolysis · NSLS · RF Body · HIFU Body · EMS · Drainage · Wraps · Drink at least 2 litres of water in the 24 hours before your session — this is not optional. Cavitation and drainage do not work properly on a dehydrated body. Eat a light meal at least 2 hours before. Do not come on a completely empty stomach or straight after a heavy meal. No alcohol for 24 hours before your session. Come with clean skin. No body lotion, oil, sunscreen or perfume on the treatment area. Remove all jewellery from and near the treatment area. Wear loose, comfortable clothing. Tell us before we start if anything has changed — new medication, pregnancy, surgery, a new medical diagnosis, or a pacemaker or implant. Drink 2.5 to 3 litres of water every day for the next 4 days. This is how your body clears the treated fat. Walk briskly or do light cardio for 20 to 30 minutes within 4 to 6 hours of your session. Massage the treated area gently for 5 minutes daily for 7 days after cavitation or cryolipolysis. Eat lightly for 24 hours — no heavy, fried or very rich meals. Mild redness, warmth, numbness or tenderness is normal and settles within a few hours to a few days. No alcohol for 72 hours. Alcohol competes with fat clearance in your liver and will reduce your result. No heavy refined carbohydrates or sugar for 72 hours. No hot shower, sauna, steam room or hot tub for 48 hours. No heavy body creams, oils or heat products on the treated area for 24 hours. Blistering,"},{"p":"ho-laserface","t":"Laser & Energy Facial Treatments — Before & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Carbon Laser Peel · Q-Switch Laser Toning · HIFU Face · RF Face · No sun exposure, sunbed or self-tan for 4 weeks before your session. Stop retinol, AHA, BHA, Vitamin C and any exfoliant 5 days before. Come with a completely clean face — no makeup, no sunscreen, no moisturiser. Tell us if you have had a cold sore, ever. We may need to prescribe an antiviral first. Tell us about every medication you take, including antibiotics and herbal supplements. No waxing or threading on the face for 48 hours before. If you have used Roaccutane (isotretinoin) in the last 6 months, we cannot treat you. Please tell us. Mild redness and warmth for 1 to 2 hours is normal. Use a gentle, fragrance-free cleanser and pat dry. Apply the calming cream we have given you. SPF 50+ every single morning, without exception, for the whole course. Small pinpoint crusts over pigment spots after Q-Switch are expected and will flake off on their own. Do NOT pick, scratch or scrub any crusting or flaking. This is what causes dark marks and scars. No makeup for 12 to 24 hours. No retinol, AHA, BHA, Vitamin C or exfoliants for 48 to 72 hours after carbon peel, or 7 days after Q-Switch. No steam, sauna, hot shower or heavy exercise for 24 hours. No direct sun for 2 weeks. Blistering or an open area appearing within 30 minutes of treatment Redness or swelling that is worse after 4 hours instead of better A cold sore appearing after treatment Pigmentation that looks darker than bef"},{"p":"ho-peel","t":"Chemical Peel — Before, During & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"All peels · Cosmelan · Yellow Peel · Start the prep products we have prescribed at least 2 weeks before a medium peel. Stop retinol, AHA, BHA and exfoliants 5 to 7 days before. No waxing, threading or hair removal on the area for 48 hours before. No sun, sunbed or self-tan for 2 weeks before. Tell us if you have ever had a cold sore. Come with a clean face — no makeup or sunscreen. Redness and a tight feeling on the day are normal. Peeling usually starts on Day 2 to 3 and lasts 3 to 5 days. Use only the post-peel cream we have given you for the first 5 days. SPF 50+ every morning, without fail. For Cosmelan or Yellow Peel: wash the mask off at exactly the time written on your card — not earlier. Do NOT pick, peel or pull at shedding skin. This causes dark marks and scarring. No sun exposure for 2 weeks. No active skincare — retinol, AHA, BHA, Vitamin C, niacinamide, scrubs — for at least 5 days. No makeup for 24 hours, or until peeling is complete after a medium peel. No steam, sauna, hot shower or exercise for 48 hours. No waxing or threading on the area for 2 weeks. No swimming pool or sea water for 1 week. No laser or IPL for at least 4 weeks. Blistering or an open wound Redness that spreads outward Pain that is severe or getting worse A cold sore outbreak Any sign of infection — pus, heat, fever"},{"p":"ho-lhr","t":"Laser Hair Removal — Before & After Your Session","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Diode LHR — all body areas · Shave the area 12 to 24 hours before your appointment. Do NOT wax, thread, pluck or epilate — the laser needs the root to be there. No sun exposure, sunbed or self-tan for 4 weeks before. Come with clean skin — no deodorant, lotion, sunscreen, perfume or makeup on the area. No alcohol for 24 hours before. Remove all jewellery from the area. If you are a new client, or your skin type is Fitzpatrick IV to VI, you must have a patch test 24 to 48 hours before your first session. Mild redness and small bumps around the hair follicles for 24 to 48 hours are normal and expected. Apply the soothing gel we have given you. SPF 50+ daily on any exposed treated area. You can shave between sessions as often as you like. Hairs will appear to grow out over the following 1 to 2 weeks before shedding — this is normal, not regrowth. Do NOT wax, thread, pluck or epilate at any point during your course. No hot shower, steam, sauna or swimming for 48 hours. No deodorant, perfume or harsh products on the area for 48 hours. No sun exposure for 2 weeks. No sunbed or self-tan for the whole course. No scratching or scrubbing the area. Blistering Significant pain that does not settle Skin that changes colour — lighter or darker Any sign of infection"},{"p":"ho-inj","t":"Injectable Treatments — Before & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Botox · Dermal Fillers · Skin Boosters · PRP · Injection Lipolysis · Avoid aspirin, ibuprofen, fish oil, Vitamin E and alcohol for 48 to 72 hours before, unless a doctor has told you to keep taking them. Tell us about every medication and supplement you take. Tell us if you have ever had a cold sore, especially before lip treatment. No dental work for 2 weeks before or after filler treatment. Come with a clean face, no makeup. Do not book injectable treatment within 2 weeks of an important event. Swelling and bruising for 3 to 7 days is normal. Use a cold compress for the first 24 hours. Sleep slightly elevated for the first 2 nights. After Botox: stay upright for 4 hours, and do not rub the area. After filler or boosters: small lumps that settle over a few days are normal. No massage or pressure on the treated area for 2 weeks unless we tell you otherwise. No sauna, steam, hot yoga or intense exercise for 48 hours. No alcohol for 24 hours. No facial, laser or energy device treatment on the area for 2 weeks. No dental work for 2 weeks after filler. URGENT — increasing pain, skin turning white, pale, blue or mottled, or a lace-like pattern on the skin after filler. Call us immediately, day or night. URGENT — any change in your vision, or pain in or around the eye after filler. Drooping of an eyelid or eyebrow after Botox Spreading redness, pus, fever, or a lump that is hot and painful"},{"p":"ho-mnrf","t":"Microneedling & MNRF — Before & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"MNRF · Derma Pen · Microneedling · Stop retinol, AHA, BHA and Vitamin C 5 days before. No sun exposure or self-tan for 2 weeks before. Tell us if you have ever had a cold sore — we will prescribe an antiviral to take before treatment. No waxing or threading on the area for 48 hours before. Come with a clean face, no makeup. Redness like sunburn for 24 to 48 hours is normal. Your skin will feel like sandpaper for 3 to 5 days as it heals. Use only the products we have given you for the first 5 days. SPF 50+ from Day 2 onward. Complete the full antiviral course if one was prescribed. No makeup for 24 hours. No active skincare for 5 to 7 days. No gym, steam, sauna or swimming for 48 to 72 hours. Do not pick or scrub the rough texture — let it shed on its own. No sun exposure for 2 weeks. Spreading redness, pus, or fever Blistering A cold sore outbreak Grid or track marks visible in the skin after healing"},{"p":"ho-hair","t":"Hair & Scalp Treatments — Before & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Hair PRP · GFC · Scalp Therapy · Mesotherapy · Trichoscopy · Wash your hair the morning of your appointment. Come with a clean, oil-free scalp. No hair oil on the day of treatment. Avoid aspirin and ibuprofen for 7 days before PRP or GFC, unless a doctor has told you to keep taking them. Eat a normal meal before your appointment — the blood draw is easier and you are less likely to feel faint. Bring your recent blood test results if you have them. Your scalp will feel tender and may swell slightly for 24 to 48 hours — this is normal. Do NOT wash your hair for 24 hours after PRP or GFC. After 24 hours, wash normally with a mild shampoo. Take any supplements we have prescribed. PRP works far better when iron, Vitamin D and thyroid are corrected. Complete the whole course — skipping sessions breaks the growth cycle. No hair colour, straightening or chemical treatment for 72 hours. No swimming, sauna or steam for 48 hours. No oil massage on the scalp for 48 hours. No ibuprofen or aspirin for 48 hours after. Do not stop your home routine as soon as the hair fall improves — that is when it comes back. Spreading redness, pus or pimples on the scalp Fever after treatment Severe headache that does not settle with paracetamol"},{"p":"ho-ht","t":"Hair Transplant — Your Complete Recovery Guide","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"FUE Hair Transplant — pre-operative and post-operative · Stop smoking 2 weeks before surgery. Smoking directly reduces how many grafts survive. No alcohol for 3 days before. Stop any blood-thinning medication only as instructed by your surgeon — never stop it on your own. Wash your hair the morning of surgery with the shampoo provided. Eat a normal breakfast on the day. Wear a shirt that buttons at the front — you must not pull clothing over your head afterwards. Arrange for someone to take you home. Sleep with your head raised at 45 degrees for the first 7 nights. Attend the Day 1 supervised wash — do not attempt the first wash alone. From Day 2, wash exactly as we demonstrated: gentle pouring, no rubbing, no direct shower pressure. Take all medication as prescribed — antibiotics, anti-inflammatories and painkillers. Swelling of the forehead around Day 2 to 4 is normal and settles by itself. The transplanted hair WILL fall out at 2 to 4 weeks. This is expected and is not a failure. Regrowth begins at 3 to 4 months. The final result is at 12 to 18 months. Keep taking the medication prescribed to protect your existing hair. Do not touch, scratch or pick the grafts or scabs. Nothing on your head — no cap, helmet or towel pressure — for 7 days unless we tell you otherwise. No smoking for 2 weeks after. No alcohol for 1 week. No gym, swimming, sauna or heavy sweating for 3 weeks. No direct sun on the scalp for 4 weeks. No hair colour or "},{"p":"ho-glp1","t":"GLP-1 Weight Management — Your Programme Guide","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Semaglutide · Tirzepatide · Complete your blood tests before your first dose — HbA1c, kidney function and liver function. Tell the doctor about every medication and supplement you take. Tell us if anyone in your family has had thyroid cancer. Tell us if you have ever had pancreatitis or gallbladder problems. Plan your protein sources before you start — this is the single most important thing you can do. Inject on the same day each week. Rotate the injection site. Store your pen in the fridge at 2 to 8°C. Do not freeze it. Eat a minimum of 60 to 80 g of protein every day. Losing muscle instead of fat is the main risk of this treatment. Eat small, slow meals. Stop at the first feeling of fullness. Do at least 150 minutes of exercise a week, and include strength training. Attend every monthly review. The dose is only increased when the current one is well tolerated. Tell any doctor, surgeon or dentist that you are on this medication before any procedure. Do not increase your dose yourself. Do not skip meals to lose faster — you will lose muscle. Avoid large, fatty or fried meals — they make nausea much worse. Avoid alcohol, which worsens nausea and low blood sugar. Do not continue this medication if you are planning a pregnancy — speak to the doctor first. Severe abdominal pain, especially going through to your back — this could be pancreatitis and needs urgent attention Pain under your right ribs — this cou"},{"p":"ho-iv","t":"IV Drip Therapy — Before & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Glutathione · Vitamin C · Antioxidant Infusions · Eat a proper meal before your appointment. Do not come fasting. Drink water before you arrive — it makes the cannula easier. Tell the doctor about every allergy you have, including food and drug allergies. Tell us if you have ever had a reaction to an injection or infusion. Tell us if you have kidney problems or a history of kidney stones. Stay for the 15-minute observation before you leave. Drink plenty of water for the rest of the day. A mild metallic taste during the infusion is normal. Keep the small dressing on for a few hours. Do not drive immediately if you felt light-headed during the infusion. Do not book infusions closer together than prescribed. Rash, hives or itching after leaving Difficulty breathing, wheezing or throat tightness — call 108 immediately Swelling of the face, lips or tongue — call 108 immediately Pain, swelling or redness at the cannula site"},{"p":"ho-thread","t":"Thread Lift — Your Recovery Guide","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"COG Threads · Mono Threads · PDO Thread Lift · No aspirin, ibuprofen, fish oil or Vitamin E for 7 days before. No alcohol for 48 hours before. No dental work for 2 weeks before. Tell us if you have ever had a cold sore. Come with a clean face, no makeup. Do not book this within 4 weeks of an important event. Sleep on your back with your head elevated for 1 week. Eat soft food for 3 to 5 days. Swelling, bruising and a tight pulling feeling for 1 to 2 weeks is normal. Take your antibiotics as prescribed. Attend your 1-week and 1-month reviews. No wide mouth opening, chewing gum, or big facial expressions for 2 weeks. No facial massage or facials for 4 weeks. No dental work for 2 weeks. No sleeping on your side or face for 1 week. No gym or sauna for 2 weeks. A thread end appearing through the skin Spreading redness, pus or fever One side of your face not moving the same as the other Severe or worsening pain"},{"p":"ho-pmu","t":"Permanent Makeup — Healing Guide","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Microblading · Machine PMU · Lip Micropigmentation · No alcohol, aspirin, ibuprofen or fish oil for 48 hours before. No caffeine on the morning of your appointment. No sun exposure, tanning or self-tan for 2 weeks before. No retinol, AHA, BHA or exfoliants near the area for 2 weeks before. For lips: if you have ever had a cold sore, you must take the antiviral we prescribe, starting before your appointment. Your patch test must have been done at least 48 hours before. Blot the area gently with clean tissue for the first day as instructed. Apply the ointment we have given you in a very thin layer as directed. The colour will look much darker and sharper for 5 to 7 days. It then flakes and lightens by around 40%. Patchiness after healing is normal — this is exactly what the touch-up is for. Attend your touch-up at 4 to 6 weeks. Your treatment is not complete without it. Do NOT pick or scratch the flaking pigment — it pulls the colour out and leaves gaps. No makeup on the area for 7 days. No swimming, sauna, steam or heavy sweating for 14 days. No sun exposure or tanning for 4 weeks. No retinol, AHA, BHA or exfoliants on or near the area for 4 weeks. Spreading redness, swelling, pus or fever A cold sore outbreak after lip treatment Itching, rash or blistering — this could be a pigment reaction"},{"p":"ho-wound","t":"After a Removal Procedure — Wound Care","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Mole · Wart · Skin Tag · Milia Removal · Biopsy · Tell us about any blood-thinning medication you take. Tell us if you scar badly or have ever had a keloid. Tell us if the mole has changed, bled or itched recently — this changes what we do. Come with a clean, makeup-free area. Keep the area clean and dry for 48 hours. Apply the ointment we have given you as directed. Let the scab fall off on its own. Use SPF 50+ on the healed area for 3 months — this is what prevents a dark mark. If a sample was sent to the lab, attend your report appointment. Do not pick or remove the scab. No swimming or sauna until fully healed. No sun exposure on the site while it heals. Do not apply any home remedy, turmeric or oil to the wound. Spreading redness, pus or fever Bleeding that does not stop with 10 minutes of gentle pressure A lump that regrows at the site A scar that becomes raised, itchy or spreads beyond the original site"},{"p":"ho-facial","t":"Facials & HydraFacial — Before & After","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"HydraFacial · Medi-Facial · Hydration Therapy · Stop retinol, AHA and BHA for 3 days before. No waxing or threading on the face for 48 hours before. Come without makeup if possible. Tell us if you have any allergy to fruit acids, aspirin or salicylates. Your skin may look pink for an hour — this settles quickly. Use a gentle cleanser for 24 hours. SPF 50+ daily. Drink plenty of water. No active skincare for 24 to 48 hours. No steam, sauna or heavy sweating for 24 hours. No makeup for 6 hours if extractions were done. A rash or hives after leaving Small red pinpoint spots that do not fade within 48 hours Any breakout that becomes painful or infected"},{"p":"ho-diet","t":"Your Nutrition Plan — How to Make It Work","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Clinical Nutrition · LIFE RISE · Come to your first consultation having eaten normally — do not diet beforehand to look better on the report. Bring a list of every medication and supplement you take. Bring any recent blood test results. Think about your real routine — work hours, who cooks, what your family eats. A plan that ignores your life will not survive the week. Log everything you eat. Honest logging beats perfect eating. Hit your protein target every single day — this is what protects your muscle while you lose fat. Weigh yourself no more than once a week, at the same time, in the same clothes. Come for your body composition analysis every 4 weeks — fat mass and muscle mass tell the real story, not the scale. Include strength training, not just cardio. Do not skip meals to speed things up. It costs you muscle and slows your metabolism. Do not go below the calorie floor we have set for you. Do not change your GLP-1 dose based on how your diet is going — only the doctor decides that. Do not judge the plan on scale weight alone. Dizziness, fainting or palpitations Losing weight much faster than planned Hair fall starting or worsening Feeling out of control around food, or anxious about eating"},{"p":"ho-tattoo","t":"Laser Tattoo Removal — Aftercare","g":"doc","s":"Client handout","k":"Q-Switch Tattoo Removal · No sun exposure or self-tan on the tattoo for 4 weeks before. Shave the area if it is hairy. Take paracetamol an hour before if you are anxious about discomfort — not ibuprofen or aspirin. Come with clean skin, no lotion or sunscreen on the tattoo. Immediate whitening, swelling and blistering is the expected response, not a complication. Keep the area clean and dry. If blisters form, apply the antibiotic ointment and a non-stick dressing, and change it daily. Once healed, use SPF 50+ on the area for the rest of the course. Your next session will be 6 to 8 weeks away — that gap is when your body actually clears the ink. Do NOT pick or pop blisters or crusts. This is the main cause of scarring. No swimming, sauna or hot tub until fully healed. No sun exposure on the area during the course. Do not ask for a shorter gap between sessions — it does not speed up removal and it increases scarring risk. Spreading redness, pus, or fever Severe pain The tattoo appearing darker after treatment rather than lighter"},{"p":"forms","t":"Laser Hair Reduction — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-LHR · FORM 07 / 08 / 09 · used for lhr"},{"p":"forms","t":"Laser Skin Rejuvenation / Scar Remodeling — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-LASERSKIN · FORM 06 · used for carbon, qswitch"},{"p":"forms","t":"Skin Peel / Chemical Peel — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-PEEL · FORM 16 · record sheet FORM 24 · used for peel, cosmelan"},{"p":"forms","t":"Botox / Botulinum Toxin — Consent & Pictorial Record","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-BOTOX · FORM 13 · used for botox"},{"p":"forms","t":"Dermal Fillers — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-FILLER · FORM 18 · hyaluronidase FORM 17 · used for filler, boosters"},{"p":"forms","t":"Thread Lift — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-THREAD · FORM 15 · used for threads"},{"p":"forms","t":"Mole / Naevus Removal — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-MOLE · FORM 19 · biopsy FORM 22 · used for lesion"},{"p":"forms","t":"Platelet Rich Plasma (PRP) — Consent & Record","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-PRP · FORM 20 · FORM 21 · used for skinprp, hairprp, gfc"},{"p":"forms","t":"Glutathione Injection / IV Drip — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-IV · FORM 23 · used for ivdrip"},{"p":"forms","t":"Micro Needle RF — Checklist & Record","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-MNRF · FORM 04 · fractional RF FORM 12 · used for mnrf, dermapen"},{"p":"forms","t":"EM Sculpt — Treatment SOP & Screening","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-EMS · FORM 02 · used for ems"},{"p":"forms","t":"General Client Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-GEN · FORM 27 · T&C FORM 25 · special consent FORM 26 · used for All treatments"},{"p":"forms","t":"Oral Isotretinoin — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Existing","k":"CF-ISO · FORM 14 · used for Dermatology prescribing"},{"p":"forms","t":"Cryolipolysis / Fat Freezing — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Gap","k":"CF-CRYO · TO BE CREATED · used for cryo"},{"p":"forms","t":"NSLS Cavitation + RF — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Gap","k":"CF-NSLS · TO BE CREATED · used for nsls"},{"p":"forms","t":"RF Body & Face Tightening — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Gap","k":"CF-RF · TO BE CREATED · used for rfbody, rfface"},{"p":"forms","t":"HIFU Body / Face & Neck — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Gap","k":"CF-HIFU · TO BE CREATED · used for hifubody, hifuface"},{"p":"forms","t":"Injection Lipolysis (Mesolipo) — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · Gap","k":"CF-INJ · TO BE CREATED · used for injlipo"},{"p":"forms","t":"GLP-1 Medical Weight Management — Consent","g":"doc","s":"Consent form · G